    {
      "note": "In 'he departed from him a little way', 'way' names the distance traversed, not a path or tract of ground: the whole measure phrase renders כִּבְרָה, headed on 'way' under rules 24 and 31. The competing joint reading with אֶרֶץ, or a split giving 'little' to the measure and 'a way' to the land, mistakes the distance sense of 'way' for a separate ground rendering; rule 30 requires the sense of every included morpheme. The margin 'some distance' corroborates this sense but is not substituted for the printed text (rule 38).",
      "source": [
        "s013"
      ],
      "source_head": "s013",
      "status": "aligned",
      "target": [
        "t014",
        "t015",
        "t016"
      ],
      "target_head": "t016"
    },
    {
      "note": "אֶרֶץ specifies the ground in the Hebrew distance expression; the ASV's 'a little way' states only the measure, with no separate or fused rendering of land or ground (rules 2 and 30).",
      "source": [
        "s014"
